{% set actor_tags_enabled = is_audio_tags_enabled(npc.UUID) %}
{% set narrator_uuid = get_narrator_uuid() %}
{% set narrator_tags_enabled = is_audio_tags_enabled(narrator_uuid) and is_narration_enabled() %}
{% set dialogue_mode = render_mode == "full" or render_mode == "transform" %}
{% set thought_mode = render_mode == "thoughts" %}
{% set has_audio_tags = actor_tags_enabled or narrator_tags_enabled %}

{% if has_audio_tags and (dialogue_mode or thought_mode) and not default(stable_split, false) %}
## Voice Performance Tags

Tags describe vocal delivery or vocal sounds, never physical actions, explanations, or internal-thought markup.

{% for voice_role in ["actor", "narrator"] %}
  {% if (voice_role == "actor" and actor_tags_enabled) or (voice_role == "narrator" and narrator_tags_enabled) %}
    {% if voice_role == "actor" %}
      {% set voice_uuid = npc.UUID %}
### Dialogue{% if thought_mode %}/thoughts{% endif %} tags
These instructions apply only to the character's dialogue{% if thought_mode %} and thoughts{% endif %}.
    {% else %}
      {% set voice_uuid = narrator_uuid %}
### Narration tags
These instructions apply only inside italicized narration.
    {% endif %}

    {% set tts_engine = get_actor_tts(voice_uuid) %}
    {% set useHiggsV3Tags = tts_engine == "higgs" or tts_engine == "higgs_v3" %}
    {% set useChatterboxTags = tts_engine == "chatterbox" %}
    {% set useFatelessTags = tts_engine == "fateless" %}
    {% set useInworld2Tags = tts_engine == "inworld" %}
    {% set useElevenlabTags = tts_engine == "elevenlabs" %}

    {% if useHiggsV3Tags %}
      {% set allowed_audio_tags = get_allowed_audio_tags(voice_uuid) %}
      {% set originalEmotionsTags = ["emotion-affection", "emotion-amusement", "emotion-anger", "emotion-arousal", "emotion-awe", "emotion-bitterness", "emotion-confusion", "emotion-contemplation", "emotion-contentment", "emotion-determination", "emotion-disgust", "emotion-elation", "emotion-enthusiasm", "emotion-fear", "emotion-helplessness", "emotion-longing", "emotion-pride", "emotion-relief", "emotion-sadness", "emotion-shame", "emotion-surprise"] %}
      {% set originalStylesTags = ["style-singing", "style-shouting", "style-whispering"] %}
      {% set originalProsodyTags = ["prosody-speed_very_slow", "prosody-speed_slow", "prosody-speed_fast", "prosody-speed_very_fast", "prosody-pitch_low", "prosody-pitch_high", "prosody-expressive_high", "prosody-expressive_low"] %}
      {% set originalSfxTags = ["sfx-cough", "sfx-laughter", "sfx-crying", "sfx-screaming", "sfx-burping", "sfx-humming", "sfx-sigh", "sfx-sniff", "sfx-sneeze"] %}
      {% set filteredEmotionsTags = "" %}
      {% set filteredStylesTags = "" %}
      {% set filteredProsodyTags = "" %}
      {% set filteredSfxTags = "" %}

      {% for tag in allowed_audio_tags %}
        {% if tag in originalEmotionsTags %}
          {% set filteredEmotionsTags = filteredEmotionsTags + "`[" + tag + "]` " %}
        {% endif %}
        {% if tag in originalStylesTags %}
          {% set filteredStylesTags = filteredStylesTags + "`[" + tag + "]` " %}
        {% endif %}
        {% if tag in originalProsodyTags %}
          {% set filteredProsodyTags = filteredProsodyTags + "`[" + tag + "]` " %}
        {% endif %}
        {% if tag in originalSfxTags %}
          {% set filteredSfxTags = filteredSfxTags + "`[" + tag + "]` " %}
        {% endif %}
      {% endfor %}

Use control tags in `[category-tag]` format to steer emotion, prosody, style, and sound effects.

**Format:** Glue each tag directly to the following tag or text, with no intervening space. Only use tags listed in the catalog below. If a category is empty, do not use tags from that category.

**Placement**
- **Emotion, style, and prosody:** Place tags at the very start of the sentence they affect. Tag the sentence once.
- **Inline SFX:** Place the tag where the sound occurs, directly before a short onomatopoeia.

**Stacking:** Use at most one tag from each category at a sentence start. Never stack two emotions, two styles, or two prosody tags. Inline SFX may be added where appropriate.

**Bare onomatopoeia needs no tag.** “Ohh,” “Mmh,” “Ugh,” and “Aah” may appear directly in the text as light vocal texture. Use an SFX tag for a distinct, emphasized sound.

**Allowed tag catalog**
- **Emotions:** {{ filteredEmotionsTags }}
- **Styles:** {{ filteredStylesTags }}
- **Prosody:** {{ filteredProsodyTags }}
- **SFX:** {{ filteredSfxTags }}

      {% if "sfx-cough" in allowed_audio_tags %}
**SFX example:** `[sfx-cough]Ahem, let's begin.`
      {% endif %}
      {% if "emotion-elation" in allowed_audio_tags and "style-whispering" in allowed_audio_tags %}
**Stacking example:** `[emotion-elation][style-whispering]You came back!`
      {% endif %}

    {% elif useChatterboxTags %}
      {% set chatterboxEmotionTags = ["[angry]", "[fear]", "[surprised]", "[whispering]", "[advertisement]", "[dramatic]", "[narration]", "[happy]", "[sarcastic]"] %}
      {% set chatterboxSoundTags = ["[clear throat]", "[sigh]", "[shush]", "[cough]", "[groan]", "[sniff]", "[gasp]", "[chuckle]", "[laugh]", "[crying]"] %}

Use [square bracket tags] to direct vocal performance.

**Allowed emotion/delivery tags:**
{{ join(chatterboxEmotionTags, ", ") }}

**Allowed sound tags:**
{{ join(chatterboxSoundTags, ", ") }}

**Usage**
- You may place one emotion/delivery tag at the beginning of an emotional sentence.
- You may insert sound tags anywhere in the line.
- Sound tags must be standalone tokens, separated from words by spaces or punctuation.
- Do not invent other bracketed text.
- Keep tags meaningful: typically 0–3 sound tags per line, unless the scene demands more.

**Examples**
- [whispering] Keep your voice down — [shush] — they'll hear us. [sigh]
- I told you not to touch that — [groan] — ever again.
- [happy] [clear throat] So… we agree? [chuckle] Great.

    {% elif useInworld2Tags or useFatelessTags %}
      {# Requires the intended TTS-2 model configuration; a saved older model_id may speak directions aloud. #}

Use natural-language [steering tags] to direct HOW speech sounds. Shape performance through **tone, pitch, emotion, volume, pace, rhythm, and vocal style**. Use the character's established speech style as the base and let emotions color it.

Make active use of tone, pitch, and tempo. Tone can be warm, cold, gentle, sharp, playful, dry, breathy, tense, soothing, seductive, commanding, or detached. Pitch may rise or fall or shift with emotion and emphasis.

Do not request slower speech or use directions that imply slower delivery, such as “slowly,” “thoughtfully,” or “carefully.” Keep speech at a natural conversational pace or faster where appropriate.

Begin every spoken sentence with a steering tag. A sentence ends at sentence-final punctuation such as `.`, `?`, or `!`; commas, semicolons, and abbreviations do not require a new tag.

**Examples**
- [speaks coldly in a low pitch with unrestrained anger] You knew.
- [speaks rapidly and playfully in a light, teasing tone with a slightly higher pitch] Still trying to catch me?
- [screeches in a frightened tone] Behind you!

Use natural [non-verbal] vocalizations where appropriate, such as [laugh], [chuckle], [giggle], [sigh], [gasp], [breathe], [cough], [clear throat], [yawn], [sniff], [groan], or [whimper]. This list is not exhaustive.

Place vocalizations after the sentence's steering tag, wherever the sound naturally occurs. Keep them separate from surrounding words.

Use punctuation for natural phrasing and occasional CAPITALS for meaningful emphasis. Avoid excessive pauses and ellipses.

    {% elif useElevenlabTags %}

Use natural-language [audio tags] to control HOW speech sounds.

Use expressive combinations of emotion, tone, pitch, volume, pace, and delivery when appropriate.

Performance tags carry forward within the same voice's passage until the performance meaningfully changes. Add a new tag when emotion, tone, intensity, pitch, pace, or vocal style changes. Do not repeat the same direction before every sentence unnecessarily.

Do not request slower speech or use tags that imply slower delivery. Keep speech at a natural conversational pace or faster where appropriate.

Use non-verbal vocalizations where appropriate, such as [laughs], [cry], [moan], [chuckles], [sighs], [exhales], [gasps], [clears throat], [snorts], or [whimpers]. This list is not exhaustive. Place them naturally within the passage, separated from surrounding words.

Use punctuation, ellipses, dashes, and occasional CAPITALS for phrasing and emphasis, while avoiding excessive pauses.

You may use accent tags when mocking or being playful.

**Examples**
- [high-pitched, whiny] Oh! I stubbed my toe [moan] on this bad navmesh! [sniffle]
- [quiet, cold] Take them to the dungeon. [cackle] You know what to do.
- [whispering, nervous] Are there spiders here? [frightened, whimpering] I don't like spiders.
- [playful, slightly higher pitch] Me? [shyly] I would never [giggle] do that.
- [angry and forceful] We will take back Skyrim and [yell] BE FREE!
- [crying] They killed my [sniff] parents, but [angry, fast] I will have my revenge!

    {% else %}

Use [square bracket tags] to direct vocal performance.

**Tag types**
- Emotions: [sad], [excited]
- Delivery: [whispers], [shouts]
- Reactions: [sighs], [laughs], [clears throat]
- Style: [dramatic tone]

Use tags sparingly: 1–2 per response for this voice.

**Example:** [sighs] I suppose you're right.

    {% endif %}
  {% endif %}
{% endfor %}

{% if not actor_tags_enabled and narrator_tags_enabled %}
Tags only work in *narration*. Do not put audio tags in dialogue or thoughts.
{% endif %}
{% if actor_tags_enabled and not narrator_tags_enabled and is_narration_enabled() %}
Tags only work in dialogue{% if thought_mode %}/thoughts{% endif %}. Do not put audio tags in *narration*.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
